<p>The U.S. Congressional Budget Office estimated Tuesday that President Trump’s proposed Golden Dome missile defense system could cost about $1.2 trillion to develop, deploy and operate over 20 years, compared with the $175 billion figure Trump gave when he announced the plan in May 2025. The CBO said it assessed a notional national missile defense architecture broadly consistent with Trump’s January 2025 executive order because the administration has not provided a detailed government plan for the system. Trump’s plan calls for a ground- and space-based shield to detect, intercept and stop missiles during major stages of an attack, including ballistic, cruise and hypersonic threats. Several reports said the plan would put weapons in space and drew attention to debate over the militarization of orbit.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/y54ym1DToHtbVBxnNtNOg4Kp0OimERCgpZFXq1Mx6VzVAZwCPFQCj5T8t3XRzBVk_4P9f_l68-fHu9UJ5eQ0Xx7bOrD5cRMsHphNQ6aa12r07CS-2NG8Jh1bthXPjnqhAjS-72z-UMkW92rYXFlrlVflHD6fT4OwjrE' alt='President Donald Trump discusses the Golden Dome from the Oval Office at the White House on May 20, 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Space costs: The space-based interceptor layer accounts for about 70% of acquisition costs and about 60% of total projected costs in the CBO estimate.</li><li>Acquisition bill: CBO put acquisition costs at just over $1 trillion, separate from operations and sustainment costs over the 20-year period.</li><li>Limited engagement: DefenseScoop reported that CBO found the notional architecture could engage limited attacks from regional adversaries such as North Korea or smaller attacks from China or Russia, but could be overwhelmed by a full-scale peer attack.</li><li>Cost comparison: Defense One reported that CBO’s estimate is roughly 15 times larger than the $79 billion the administration plans to spend from the Golden Dome for America account over five years.</li></ul><blockquote>The system would provide significantly expanded defensive capabilities but would not be impenetrable, particularly against large-scale attacks from peer adversaries - Congressional Budget Office</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Congressional Budget Office: CBO said the gap between its estimate and public administration figures could reflect differences in scope, time frame and assumptions, according to Defense One. (<a href='https://www.defenseone.com/defense-systems/2026/05/golden-dome-cost-trillion-cbo/413485/'>Defense One</a>)</li><li>President Trump: Trump said in his executive order that the threat from next-generation strategic weapons had become more intense and complex over the previous 40 years. (<a href='https://www.elfinanciero.com.mx/mundo/2026/05/12/cupula-dorada-de-trump-costara-12-billones-de-dolares-la-cifra-inicial-era-de-175-mil-mdd/'>El Financiero</a>)</li><li>Office of Golden Dome for America: Program director Mike Guetlein estimated in March that Golden Dome would cost about $185 billion, below the CBO’s notional estimate. (<a href='https://defence-industry.eu/congressional-budget-office-estimates-golden-dome-missile-defense-system-could-cost-1-2-trillion/'>Defence Industry Europe</a>)</li><li>Some experts: La Nación reported that some experts had called the project unrealistic and redundant because of existing U.S. missile-defense systems. (<a href='https://www.nacion.com/el-mundo/la-cupula-dorada-de-trump-podria-costar-12/UFHTKNDBIZB55GIS7HDLV4WIXU/story/'>La Nación</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/trump%27s-proposed-%27golden-dome%27-estimated-to-cost-1.2-trillion-far-more-than-he-initially-said'>Trump&#x27;s proposed &#x27;Golden Dome&#x27; estimated to cost $1.2 trillion, far more than he initially said</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/trump-golden-dome-missile-shield-could-cost-1-2-trillion-over-20-years-11486815#publisher=newsstand'>Trump &#x27;Golden Dome&#x27; Missile Shield Could Co